        {
          "id": 2144562038,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "In principle there are likely various other cases where the GSMTAP radio related fields make no sense.  For example if it's E1/T1/ISDN payload, where there is no \"receive level\" \"antenna number\" or the like.  It's a constraint of the historic growth of GSMTAPv2, and it shows the need for a GSMTAPv3 successor that has been discussed on and off for many years by now, but nobody found the time to actually implement it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 357252,
            "username": "laf0rge",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Harald Welte",
            "state": "active",
